BoringSSL for dc_proxy
======================

dc_proxy links BoringSSL statically because it needs the RFC 9345
Delegated-Credential *server* API, which the stock TLS stacks do not expose.
BoringSSL is not vendored here; build it once from the pinned commit plus the
patch in this directory, then point the Makefile at the checkout.

  Base commit: d258906c992e30c07328eac375f2c6a4a0f30fd9
  Patch:       boringssl-dc.patch   (apply on top of that commit)

Easiest: run `./fetch_boringssl.sh` (clones the pinned commit into ./boringssl,
applies the patch, and builds the static libs), then `make`.

Equivalent manual steps (from this directory):

  git clone https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl
  cd boringssl
  git checkout d258906c992e30c07328eac375f2c6a4a0f30fd9
  git apply ../boringssl-dc.patch
  cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build build
  cd ..
  make                       # builds dc_proxy against ./boringssl

The Makefile defaults to BORINGSSL=./boringssl (gitignored) and expects the
static libraries at $(BORINGSSL)/build/{libssl,libcrypto}.a. Use a checkout
elsewhere with `make BORINGSSL=/path/to/boringssl`.
